        "original_id": "a35c096e-e9d4-5ba8-8161-558370219777",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Howard Hawks, Arthur Berthelet, Katharine Hepburn, Cary Grant\n- Works: Bringing Up Baby\n- Companies: RKO Radio Pictures\n- Roles: film director, producer, screenwriter\n- Topics: classic Hollywood era, silent movies, stage plays, Broadway, screwball comedy film\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Berthelet (1879–1949) was an American film director who moved from directing stage plays, including several on Broadway, to directing silent movies.\n- Howard Winchester Hawks (May 30, 1896–December 26, 1977) was an American film director, producer, and screenwriter of the classic Hollywood era.\n- Bringing Up Baby is a 1938 American screwball comedy film directed by Howard Hawks.\n- Bringing Up Baby stars Katharine Hepburn and Cary Grant.\n- RKO Radio Pictures released Bringing Up Baby.",
